  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting safe and sustainable access to basic primary health services for conflict- and violence-affected communities in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict-affected people have uninterrupted access to quality preventive and curative basic health care services, even during emergency situations. Conflict-affected people, in particular children and pregnant and lactating women, benefit from healthcare services provided by skilled health staff, at well-equipped facilities. Health staff, including midwives, are given training and other support to improve their skills and ability to provide good-quality health care.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conflict-affected people, in particular children and pregnant and lactating women, receive preventive and curative health care that meets national/international standards.&#xbcf4;&#xac74;&#xc758;&#xb8cc;&#xc11c;&#xbe44;&#xc2a4;&#xc5d0; &#xb300;&#xd55c; &#xc811;&#xadfc;&#xc131; &#xc81c;&#xace0;, &#xc591;&#xc9c8;&#xc758; &#xbcf4;&#xac74;&#xc758;&#xb8cc; &#xc11c;&#xbe44;&#xc2a4; &#xc81c;&#xacf5;, &#xbcf4;&#xac74;&#xc758;&#xb8cc;&#xc778;&#xb825;&#xc758; &#xc5ed;&#xb7c9;&#xac15;&#xd654;</narrative>
  </description>
